hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21015","Yunus and Affan narrated to us, they said: Ghassan ibn Burzin narrated to us, Sayyar ibn Salamah al-Riyahi narrated to us, from al-Bara al-Saliti, from Nuqadah al-Asadi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent Nuqadah al-Asadi to a man to ask him for the loan of a she-camel of his, and the man turned him away, so he sent him to another man besides him, and he sent him a she-camel. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Nuqadah coming leading it, he said: O Allah, bless it and bless the one who sent it. Nuqadah said: O Messenger of Allah, and the one who brought it? He said: and the one who brought it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded it and it was milked and it yielded milk. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, increase the wealth and children of so-and-so, meaning the first one who refused. O Allah, make the provision of so-and-so day by day, meaning the owner of the she-camel who sent it."
